                <pb facs="0289" n="1249" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1249"/>

                <head>No. 833.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Romero to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Mexico</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 1, 1887</date>.
                        (Received November 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Personal.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Bayard</hi>: I have the honor to inform
                    you that I have this day received a letter from the consul of the United States
                    of Mexico at El Paso, Texas, bearing date of the 27th ultimo, whereby lie
                    informs me that the horses claimed by Colonel Cowart as belonging to the United
                    States Government were delivered to that officer on the 22d, at Paso del Norte,
                    Mexico.</p>
                <p>In order that the delivery might be made without further delay, and since certain
                    formalities had to be complied with for the purpose of proving the ownership of
                    the horses, the political chief of the canton of Paso del Norte gave his
                    personal bond to the court of that canton, in order that the horses might be
                    given up.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Romero.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
